From 5030dfcd1bc95901d27f21f467704841374971af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:42:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arp freeze from the community's open PR #5208: what the arp
 plays written into the clip as notes, the arp off, undo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports "Add arp freeze" by Loïc Wisniewski (SynthstromAudible/DelugeFirmware#5208, commit 9641fbb31, 25.10.2026, still
open and planned for 1.4) onto v1.3 with mastertune's features. Its new files (model/clip/arp_freeze.*, the freeze
confirmation, the menu item, two consequences for the undo) as they are; the glue merged with steps 1 to 6 (strings,
the community features' list, the arpeggiator's clock checks in mastertune's render()).

- FREEZE at the end of the arp's Pattern menu (synth, MIDI and CV clips, the kit arp), with a confirmation: the notes
  that feed the arp are replaced by the notes it plays, the arp is switched off, as one undoable action. The real
  arpeggiator is run tick by tick over the clip outside playback, on a copy of its settings; reversed and ping-pong
  clips are written out as they sound. Community features > Arp Freeze switches it off.
- For mastertune's ratchets (fixed counts, bounce, roll, ball, a ratchet over several steps), two changes to the
  freeze's loop: while a ratchet runs, render() is run at every subtick (16 a tick), as the audio buffers run it when
  playing, and each hit or note-off goes to its nearest tick; and a ratchet's next step (the tick resets gatePos
  without a note-on) starts the gate's count anew, as a new note does. Without them the hits of a ratchet lasting
  several steps piled up at the start of each step.
- Four faults found by the review of the port, in the freeze's loop: a hit rounded onto the next step's note at the
  same key could make the unstable sort drop the step's note instead of the hit (now the shorter note goes, and no hit
  is rounded past the clip's end); the audio was kept going every 1,024 ticks, though a ratchet's ticks now render 16
  times (now by the work done); render() got no phase increment, so a hit due just before a ratchet's next step was
  dropped where playing keeps it; and with mastertune's latch the frozen clip started without the notes the arp has
  latched from the clip's end when it loops (now a first pass, not recorded, leaves the arp as it is from the second
  loop on).
